* Murata OKI-78SR-5/1.5 behavioral model (switching regulator, averaged)
* Output: ideal 5 V source that sags when IN drops below ~7 V (2 V headroom).
* Input: constant-power load, I_in = P_out / (eff * V_in) + no-load current (datasheet: 5 mA typ),
* so input current rises as the bulk cap sags, like a real buck converter.
* Does not model switching ripple, soft-start or undervoltage lockout.
.subckt OKI78SR5 IN GND OUT params: vout=5 eff=0.85 hdrm=2 iq=5m
Bout OUTI GND V={min(vout, max(V(IN,GND)-hdrm, 0))}
Vsns OUTI OUT 0
Bin IN GND I={V(OUT,GND)*max(i(Vsns),0)/(eff*max(V(IN,GND),1)) + iq*min(V(IN,GND),1)}
Rleak IN GND 10Meg
.ends
